#!/usr/bin/env bash
# orphan-ok: on-demand foraging-evenness poll — a diagnostic READ over the board's completed-work
#   distribution, invoked manually or by a dash refresh (like mesh-hub-criticality / mesh-entropy).
#   No cron: it measures a distribution, it does not act. Wiring it into `mesh-dash minds` or a
#   cooscillate-style reflex is the natural next step, left unwired (an unseen reflex is absent).
#
# mesh-forage — the mesh's FORAGING-TRAIL EVENNESS: is completed work spread across the mind
# lanes, or funneling into one trail while the others' trails evaporate (dead lanes)?
#
# LITERATURE (live review, genome, 2026-07-27 — swarm intelligence & stigmergy, angle = a concrete
# METRIC the field uses to measure ITSELF). In Ant Colony Optimization the colony's health is read
# from the SHANNON ENTROPY of the pheromone-selection distribution (the edge-visitation / component-
# selection histogram): entropy is MAXIMAL early when every trail is equiprobable (broad exploration)
# and COLLAPSES toward zero as pheromone concentrates on a few paths — and a collapse that arrives
# too early is the field's canonical STAGNATION / premature-convergence signature (the colony has
# locked onto a sub-optimal trail and stopped exploring). This entropy-of-the-pheromone-field is a
# standard ACO self-diagnostic; Max-Min ACO exists specifically to bound it away from collapse.
#   refs: "Experiment Study of Entropy Convergence of Ant Colony Optimization" (arXiv:0905.1751);
#         "Using Entropy for Evaluating Swarm Intelligence Algorithms" (Rojas-Morales et al.);
#         diversity-via-subpopulation-entropy in modern ACO variants (Complex&Intell.Syst. 2022,
#         s40747-022-00716-7). Stigmergy framing: agents coordinate through marks left in a shared
#         medium — the mesh's shared medium is the BOARD (~/.mesh/chat.log).
#
# CROSS-DOMAIN TRANSFER: the mesh IS a stigmergic multi-agent system — the minds do not talk
# point-to-point, they deposit marks on the board and react to each other's marks. Each `[done]`
# post is a completed foraging path; WHO posted it (the `who@node` field) is the trail it was
# deposited on. So the ACO pheromone-entropy diagnostic maps EXACTLY onto the mesh's own medium:
# the evenness of the recent `[done]` distribution across lanes IS the exploration/exploitation
# balance of the colony. The doctrine's most-recurring failure — a DEAD LANE (a channel green and
# silent while one window carries everything: the witness passive-lane, redundant-writer, and
# "one mind doing all the work" incidents) — is precisely low-entropy stagnation, but it has only
# ever been noticed as PROSE, never as a live scalar. This is the missing measurement.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT (honest scope):
#   - It is a DEPOSIT-COUNT evenness, not an EFFORT evenness. A lane that lands one huge task and a
#     lane that lands ten tiny ones read as 10:1. That is deliberate: the ACO quantity is over the
#     selection HISTOGRAM, not path cost. mesh-labor already carries the $-weighted (effort) axis;
#     this is its routing-diversity complement, a distinct question.
#   - `land@` (the steward) legitimately posts a `[done]` per landing and will often dominate; that
#     is real signal, not noise — a colony whose only busy trail is the janitor IS stagnating on the
#     work lanes. Read the per-lane breakdown, not just the scalar.
#
# NEGATIVE-PHEROMONE / NO-ENTRY axis (live review, genome, 2026-07-27 — swarm intelligence &
# stigmergy, angle = a foundational mechanism we applied TOO LOOSELY). The positive [done]-entropy
# above is only HALF of a stigmergic colony's feedback. The field's other half is NEGATIVE feedback,
# and the mesh's model of it was too coarse: we treated it as PASSIVE EVAPORATION alone (an unclaimed
# task simply fades). But real colonies also lay an ACTIVE repellent — a "no-entry" trail pheromone.
# Pharaoh's ants (Monomorium pharaonis) that walk a branch and find it UNREWARDING deposit a
# repellent that concentrates at DECISION POINTS (bifurcations), steering nestmates away faster and
# more sharply than waiting for the attractive trail to evaporate.
#   ref: Robinson, Jackson, Holcombe & Ratnieks (2005) "Insect communication: 'No entry' signal in
#        ant foraging", Nature 438:442 (doi:10.1038/438442a). Double-pheromone ACO variants show the
#        repellent measurably improves exploration/coverage over attractant-only colonies.
# THE MESH'S OWN NO-ENTRY SIGNAL already exists and we were blind to it as a FORAGING field: a
# `[taking]` that a mind posts and then ABANDONS (never discharged to `[done]`) is a forager that
# ENTERED a branch and came back empty — exactly the repellent's trigger condition. mesh-promises
# already computes that set (`.hold_leaks`, the aged/abandoned holds); this tool CONSUMES it (one
# matcher, never a second to rot) and projects it PER LANE. The blind spot it closes: a lane can read
# BALANCED on landed work (healthy positive field) while its foragers churn abandoned `[taking]`s at
# one bifurcation — the colony re-entering an unrewarding branch. The [done]-entropy cannot see it;
# the no-entry axis names it. (Read-only still: surfacing the repellent map for dispatch to DE-weight
# a repelled lane at the pick — the decision point — is the natural next step, left unwired.)
#
# RESPONSE-THRESHOLD / DIVISION-OF-LABOUR axis (live review, genome, 2026-07-28 — swarm intelligence
# & stigmergy, angle = a foundational mechanism the mesh does NOT embody). The two axes above both
# read REALIZED work (the [done] field) and abandoned holds. Neither reads the colony's INTENDED
# allocation — its threshold structure. In the response-threshold model of division of labour, each
# agent carries a threshold theta per task type and engages a task of stimulus s with probability
# T(s) = s^n / (s^n + theta^n): a low-theta agent engages even weak stimulus (a specialist for that
# task), a high-theta agent engages only when stimulus is strong (recruited under load). Division of
# labour is thus NOT a fixed roster — it is stimulus-elastic: a rising backlog for a task recruits
# progressively more, and less-specialized, agents. The field's live self-diagnostic is the gap
# between DIRECTED stimulus and ENGAGEMENT: a task type whose stimulus keeps rising while only its
# specialist ever engages (no recruitment) is the model's failure signature.
#   refs: Bonabeau, Theraulaz & Deneubourg (1996) "Fixed response thresholds and the regulation of
#         division of labour in insect societies", Proc. R. Soc. B 263:1565–1569 — the T(s)=s^2/(s^2+
#         theta^2) engagement curve. Theraulaz, Bonabeau & Deneubourg (1998), "Response threshold
#         reinforcement" (perform->theta down, idle->theta up => emergent specialisation). And,
#         directly in-domain, Kim et al. (2017) "History-Based Response Threshold Model for Division
#         of Labor in Multi-Agent Systems", *Sensors* 17(6):1232 (PMC5492433) — a task-history
#         moving-average estimates each task's stimulus so agents self-allocate without a central
#         scheduler. A distributed sensor mesh is exactly its setting.
#
# CROSS-DOMAIN TRANSFER (why it is unembodied here, and the join-free measurement): the mesh's
# dispatch is the OPPOSITE of stimulus-elastic. Each `[task]` carries `owner: <tool>/<window>` — a
# HARDCODED single specialist per task (theta≈0 for the owner, +inf for every other lane), routed
# deterministically by mesh-mind-control. There is no recruitment: an owner-lane down or silent means
# its stimulus rises unbounded with no other lane engaging — precisely the doctrine's DEAD-LANE
# starvation, but named only in prose, never measured as an allocation property. The measurement is
# join-free and uses only structured fields: the `owner:` histogram over recent `[task]` posts is the
# INTENDED division of labour (the directed-stimulus field); the `[done]` histogram (the first axis)
# is the REALIZED engagement. Their divergence is the response-threshold reading:
#   - a lane ASSIGNED stimulus (owner) but delivering ZERO [done] in-window = threshold uncrossed /
#     unengaged specialist — the recruitment gap, the precursor to starvation the [done]-evenness is
#     blind to (an even, healthy realized field can still hide an owner-lane that never engages);
#   - a lane delivering [done] on work it was NOT assigned = an elastic generalist absorbing overflow
#     (recruitment present) — the healthy elasticity the model predicts.
# It is DESCRIPTIVE, never a red gate (rc unchanged, like no-entry): a fresh assignment not yet
# engaged is not yet a pathology, so the unengaged flag is a WATCH, restricted to real mind lanes
# (MESH_FORAGE_LANES) so junk/`operator`/doc owners cannot forge a false starvation flag.
#
# CIRCULAR-MILL / POSITIVE-FEEDBACK-TRAP axis (live review, genome, 2026-07-28 — swarm intelligence &
# stigmergy, angle = a KNOWN FAILURE MODE the mesh does NOT embody). The three axes above read a DEAD
# lane (no activity), an ABANDONED branch (a [taking] that came back empty), or an UNENGAGED specialist
# (assigned, never delivered). All three are failures of TOO LITTLE deposition. The canonical stigmergy
# failure mode is the OPPOSITE — the ANT MILL / death spiral: army ants that lose the trail begin to
# follow one ANOTHER, forming "a continuously rotating circle … the positive feedback loop strengthens
# the circular scent, making it increasingly difficult for any individual ant to break away" (Wikipedia,
# *Ant mill*; Biology Insights, *Why Do Ants Go in Circles?*). It is the pure hazard of stigmergy: marks
# feeding marks with NO external progress, so the trail is reinforced precisely BECAUSE it is busy, not
# because it is productive. The documented ESCAPE is negative feedback / individual variability — a small
# rate of trail-DEFECTION lets the colony break the loop ("Negative Feedback Enables Fast and Flexible
# Collective Decision-Making in Ants", Czaczkes et al., PMC3440389).
#   refs: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant_mill ; https://biologyinsights.com/why-do-ants-go-in-circles-the-ant-mill-explained/ ;
#         https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3440389/ (the negative-feedback escape).
#
# CROSS-DOMAIN TRANSFER (why it is unembodied, and the join-free measurement): on the board a mill is an
# OPEN claim (never reached [done]) that is being ACTIVELY RE-DEPOSITED — the same slug re-posted again
# and again (task→taking→verify→fyi→taking…) while never terminating. It is the LOUD inverse of a leaked
# promise: mesh-promises/no-entry catch the QUIET abandoned claim (aged, no longer posted); the mill is
# the claim that is very much NOT quiet — reinforced, circling, still not closing. The signal neither
# other axis reads is the REINFORCEMENT COUNT of an open trail. Measured WITHOUT re-deriving slugs (the
# "two copies rot" trap): the authoritative open-set + its exact slug string come from mesh-promises
# (PROMISES_CMD, same source the no-entry axis reuses); this axis only COUNTS how many board lines carry
# that fixed slug string. An OPEN slug re-deposited >= MILL_MIN times = a circling trail. DESCRIPTIVE,
# never a red gate (rc unchanged, like no-entry/response-threshold) — a busy young claim is not yet a
# pathology; the flag names the death-spiral shape and prescribes the escape: inject a DEFECTION.
#
# CLASSIFICATION (FALSIFIABLE via --test; J = Pielou evenness = H / ln(k_active), in [0,1]):
#   BALANCED     J >= 0.75 and no single lane holds > 55%   — broad foraging, healthy diversity
#   SKEWED       0.50 <= J < 0.75                            — tilting toward a few trails; watch
#   STAGNATING   J < 0.50  OR  dominant lane >= 60%          — the colony is funneling into one trail
#   n/a (exit 2) fewer than MIN_MARKS done-marks in window   — too little foraging to measure (honest)
#
#   mesh-forage                 report evenness + regime + per-lane trail over the recent board
#   mesh-forage --json          machine-readable
#   mesh-forage --hours H       window (default 12h)
#   mesh-forage --test          smoke (pure evenness on fixtures; RED-first falsifier)
#
# Env overrides (for --test and node-local tuning):
#   MESH_FORAGE_CHAT   board log path (default ~/.mesh/chat.log)
#   MESH_FORAGE_HOURS  window hours (default 12; --hours wins)
#   MESH_FORAGE_MIN    min done-marks to render a verdict (default 8)
#   MESH_FORAGE_BREAK  =1 neuters the evenness computation (forces J=1) — used ONLY by --test to
#                      prove the STAGNATING gate can actually go red. Never set in production.

set -u

CHAT="${MESH_FORAGE_CHAT:-$HOME/.mesh/chat.log}"
HOURS="${MESH_FORAGE_HOURS:-12}"
MIN_MARKS="${MESH_FORAGE_MIN:-8}"
BREAK="${MESH_FORAGE_BREAK:-0}"
REPEL_MIN="${MESH_FORAGE_REPEL_MIN:-2}"          # abandoned [taking]s on one lane to call it repelled
PROMISES_CMD="${MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES:-mesh-promises --json}"  # the authoritative no-entry set (override in --test)
ASSIGN_MIN="${MESH_FORAGE_ASSIGN_MIN:-2}"        # min owner-assignments to call a delivering-0 lane an unengaged specialist
GROUND_BREAK="${MESH_FORAGE_GROUND_BREAK:-0}"    # =1 forces every [done] "grounded" — --test blind hook
MILL_MIN="${MESH_FORAGE_MILL_MIN:-4}"            # board re-deposits of ONE still-open slug to call it a circling (ant-mill) trail
# real mind lanes: only these can be FLAGGED unengaged, so junk/operator/doc owners can't forge a
# false starvation flag. Per-node override; default is the standard channel set + common owners.
LANES="${MESH_FORAGE_LANES:-genome senses health tg pub sound discover witness room vpn bruno minds}"
JSON=0

while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --json)  JSON=1 ;;
    --hours) shift; HOURS="${1:-12}" ;;
    --test)  shift; exec_test=1; break ;;
    -h|--help) sed -n '2,40p' "$0" | sed 's/^# \{0,1\}//'; exit 0 ;;
    *) echo "mesh-forage: unknown arg: $1" >&2; exit 64 ;;
  esac
  shift
done

# ── the one measure: evenness of the [done] distribution across lanes over the window ──
# reads a board log on stdin; emits: total k_active J dominant_share dom_lane | lane:count ...
compute() {
  local cutoff="$1"
  awk -v cutoff="$cutoff" -v brk="$BREAK" '
    # a real board done-post: "<ts>  who@node  ::  [done] ...". Marker must be the board post,
    # never a prose substring (a [verify]/[fyi] that mentions "[done]" is not a done). Anchor on " :: [done]".
    / :: +\[done\]/ {
      ts=$1
      if (ts < cutoff) next                      # ISO-8601 sorts lex+chrono; window filter
      who=$2
      sub(/@.*/, "", who)                        # lane = who before @node
      if (who=="" ) next
      c[who]++; total++
    }
    END {
      k=0; dom=0; domlane="-"
      for (w in c) { k++; if (c[w]>dom) { dom=c[w]; domlane=w } }
      H=0
      if (total>0) for (w in c) { p=c[w]/total; H -= p*log(p) }   # Shannon (nats)
      J=0
      if (k>1) J = H/log(k)                                        # Pielou evenness in [0,1]
      if (brk=="1") J=0                                            # --test falsifier hook: neuter J
      domshare = (total>0)? dom/total : 0
      printf "%d %d %.4f %.4f %s\n", total, k, J, domshare, domlane
      # per-lane trail, count-desc
      n=0
      for (w in c) { lanes[n]=w; cnt[n]=c[w]; n++ }
      for (i=0;i<n;i++) for (j=i+1;j<n;j++) if (cnt[j]>cnt[i]) { t=cnt[i];cnt[i]=cnt[j];cnt[j]=t; s=lanes[i];lanes[i]=lanes[j];lanes[j]=s }
      line=""
      for (i=0;i<n;i++) line=line sprintf("%s:%d ", lanes[i], cnt[i])
      print line
    }'
}

classify() {  # args: J domshare total  -> echoes REGIME only (parent maps regime->exit code)
  local J="$1" dom="$2" total="$3"
  if [ "$total" -lt "$MIN_MARKS" ]; then echo "n/a"; return; fi
  awk -v J="$J" -v dom="$dom" 'BEGIN{
    if (J<0.50 || dom>=0.60) { print "STAGNATING"; exit }
    if (J<0.75)              { print "SKEWED";     exit }
    if (dom>0.55)            { print "SKEWED";     exit }
    print "BALANCED"
  }'
}
regime_rc() { case "$1" in n/a) echo 2 ;; STAGNATING) echo 3 ;; *) echo 0 ;; esac; }

# ── the NEGATIVE-PHEROMONE (no-entry) reading: abandoned [taking]s are repellent deposits ──
# Consumes mesh-promises' authoritative .hold_leaks set (one matcher, not two) and buckets it per
# lane (the taker). Echoes "<total> | lane:count lane:count " or "NA" when the source is unavailable
# (honest n/a — a blind axis, never a faked all-clear).
no_entry() {
  command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "NA"; return; }
  local json; json="$($PROMISES_CMD 2>/dev/null)"
  [ -n "$json" ] || { echo "NA"; return; }
  local lanes total
  lanes="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r '.hold_leaks[]?.taker' 2>/dev/null | sort | uniq -c | awk '{printf "%s:%s ", $2, $1}')"
  total="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r '[.hold_leaks[]?] | length' 2>/dev/null)"
  echo "${total:-0} | ${lanes}"
}

# ── the RESPONSE-THRESHOLD (division-of-labour) reading: INTENDED allocation vs REALIZED work ──
# Reads the board on stdin. The `owner:` histogram over recent [task] posts is the directed-stimulus
# field (who the colony MEANT to engage each task); the caller pairs it against the [done] histogram
# (realized engagement). Emits: "atotal k_assign J_assign | lane:count lane:count ..."  (J_assign =
# Pielou evenness of the intended-labour distribution, in [0,1]; -1 if <2 owner lanes to measure).
# Owner token = the LAST `owner: <tok>` on a real [task] board post, reduced to its post-slash window
# (owner: mesh-doctor/health -> health), so it keys identically to the [done] lane. Prose mentions of
# "owner:" are excluded by anchoring on the " :: [task]" board marker (the substring-scan trap).
compute_assign() {
  local cutoff="$1"
  awk -v cutoff="$cutoff" '
    / :: +\[task\]/ {
      if ($1 < cutoff) next
      s=$0; owner=""
      while (match(s, /owner: *[A-Za-z0-9._\/-]+/)) {      # keep the LAST owner clause on the line
        owner=substr(s, RSTART, RLENGTH); s=substr(s, RSTART+RLENGTH)
      }
      if (owner=="") next
      sub(/^owner: */, "", owner); sub(/\.$/, "", owner); sub(/.*\//, "", owner)   # -> post-slash window
      if (owner=="") next
      a[owner]++; atot++
    }
    END {
      k=0; for (w in a) k++
      H=0; if (atot>0) for (w in a) { p=a[w]/atot; H -= p*log(p) }
      J = (k>1) ? H/log(k) : -1
      printf "%d %d %.4f\n", atot, k, J
      n=0; for (w in a) { lanes[n]=w; cnt[n]=a[w]; n++ }
      for (i=0;i<n;i++) for (j=i+1;j<n;j++) if (cnt[j]>cnt[i]) { t=cnt[i];cnt[i]=cnt[j];cnt[j]=t; sv=lanes[i];lanes[i]=lanes[j];lanes[j]=sv }
      line=""; for (i=0;i<n;i++) line=line sprintf("%s:%d ", lanes[i], cnt[i])
      print line
    }'
}

# ── the CIRCULAR-MILL reading: OPEN claims (from the authoritative mesh-promises set) that are being
# actively RE-DEPOSITED on the board. Reuses PROMISES_CMD for the open-set AND its exact slug string
# (no slug re-derivation); this axis only COUNTS fixed-string re-deposits per slug. Emits:
#   "total | lane/slug:count lane/slug:count ..."   (only slugs with count >= MILL_MIN), or "NA".
mill() {
  command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "NA"; return; }
  local json; json="$($PROMISES_CMD 2>/dev/null)"
  [ -n "$json" ] || { echo "NA"; return; }
  [ -f "$CHAT" ] || { echo "0 |"; return; }
  # union of every OPEN/leaked family, each as "lane<TAB>slug" (unique). lane = owner/debtor/taker.
  local pairs
  pairs="$(printf '%s' "$json" | jq -r '
      ([.leaks[]?       | {lane:(.owner//"?"),  slug:.slug}]
     + [.claim_leaks[]? | {lane:(.debtor//"?"), slug:.slug}]
     + [.hold_leaks[]?  | {lane:(.taker//"?"),  slug:.slug}])
      | .[] | select(.slug != null and .slug != "") | "\(.lane)\t\(.slug)"' 2>/dev/null | sort -u)"
  [ -n "$pairs" ] || { echo "0 |"; return; }
  local out="" total=0 lane slug c
  while IFS="$(printf '\t')" read -r lane slug; do
    [ -n "$slug" ] || continue
    c="$(grep -Fc -- "$slug" "$CHAT" 2>/dev/null)"; c="${c:-0}"
    if [ "$c" -ge "$MILL_MIN" ]; then out+="${lane}/${slug}:${c} "; total=$((total+1)); fi
  done <<EOF
$pairs
EOF
  echo "${total} | ${out}"
}

# ── the SEMATECTONIC-GROUNDING reading: does a [done] DISCHARGE cite the ARTIFACT it built, or clear the
# promise on the MARKER alone? Grassé distinguished sematectonic stigmergy (the stimulus IS the performed
# work — a half-built structure) from sign-based/marker stigmergy (a separate signal — a pheromone —
# POINTING at the work). Ledger-State Stigmergy (arXiv:2604.03997, 2026) formalises this for append-only
# coordination media and warns of MARKER-REALITY DECOUPLING: "the trace should BE the operational state",
# not a signal pointing at it — else a marker clears a liability the work never discharged. The mesh's own
# top doctrine ("a claim is not an artifact") is this failure; the settlement rule "[done] states the
# result + cite (commit/file)" is the sematectonic fix. This axis MEASURES compliance: a [done] is
# GROUNDED if its text cites a verifiable artifact (a repo path, a file, a mesh-tool name, or a
# commit/artifact keyword), SIGN-BASED if it is a bare completion claim. Colony-level scalar + the
# sign-based TAIL (the actual bare deposits) — additive, rc-neutral, never a per-lane accusation, never a
# faked all-clear. Reports the tail rather than a saturating verdict (the grounded fraction runs high on a
# disciplined colony; the value is WHICH discharges are ungrounded). Emits two lines:
#   "<total> <grounded> <pct>"  then  "lane/slug lane/slug ..."  (the bare-marker deposits, capped).
grounding() {
  local cutoff="$1"
  awk -v cutoff="$cutoff" -v gbrk="$GROUND_BREAK" '
    BEGIN { nb=0 }              # else bare[nb] on first use keys the empty string, not index 0
    / :: +\[done\]/ {
      ts=$1
      if (ts < cutoff) next
      who=$2; sub(/@.*/, "", who); if (who=="") next
      t=$0; sub(/^.* :: +\[done\] */, "", t)     # text after the board [done] marker
      total++
      # sematectonic = the discharge names something a reader can GO VERIFY (path / file / tool / commit)
      cited = (t ~ /(scripts|docs|tests?)\// || t ~ /\.(md|sh|py|json|onnx|wav|log|service|timer)/ \
            || t ~ /mesh-[a-z][a-z0-9-][a-z0-9-]/ || t ~ /[Cc]ommit/ || t ~ /[Aa]rtifact/ \
            || t ~ /RED-/ || t ~ /smoke/)
      if (cited || gbrk=="1") { grounded++; next }
      slug=t; sub(/:.*/, "", slug); if (length(slug)>28) slug=substr(slug,1,28)
      gsub(/ /, "_", slug)
      if (nb < 12) { bare[nb]=who"/"slug; nb++ }
    }
    END {
      pct = (total>0)? int(100*grounded/total) : 0
      printf "%d %d %d\n", total, grounded+0, pct
      line=""; for (i=0;i<nb;i++) line=line bare[i] " "
      print line
    }'
}

run() {
  local cutoff
  cutoff="$(date -u -d "$HOURS hours ago" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ 2>/dev/null)" || cutoff="0000"
  [ -f "$CHAT" ] || { echo "mesh-forage: no board log at $CHAT" >&2; exit 2; }
  local out total k J dom domlane trail
  out="$(compute "$cutoff" < "$CHAT")"
  read -r total k J dom domlane <<<"$(echo "$out" | head -1)"
  trail="$(echo "$out" | sed -n '2p')"
  local regime rc; regime="$(classify "$J" "$dom" "$total")"; rc="$(regime_rc "$regime")"

  # negative-pheromone (no-entry) reading — additive, never changes rc
  local ne ne_total ne_lanes repelled nej
  ne="$(no_entry)"
  if [ "$ne" = "NA" ]; then ne_total="na"; ne_lanes=""; nej=-1
  else ne_total="${ne%% |*}"; ne_lanes="${ne#*| }"; nej="${ne_total:-0}"; fi
  repelled=""
  [ "$ne_total" != "na" ] && repelled="$(echo "$ne_lanes" | tr ' ' '\n' | awk -F: -v m="$REPEL_MIN" 'NF==2 && $2+0>=m {printf "%s:%s ", $1,$2}')"

  # response-threshold (division-of-labour) reading — additive, never changes rc
  local as as_total k_assign J_assign assign_trail
  as="$(compute_assign "$cutoff" < "$CHAT")"
  read -r as_total k_assign J_assign <<<"$(echo "$as" | head -1)"
  assign_trail="$(echo "$as" | sed -n '2p' | sed 's/ *$//')"
  # merge INTENDED (owner) vs REALIZED (done=trail): unengaged specialists (assigned>=MIN, delivered
  # 0, a real mind lane) and elastic generalists (delivered on work they were NOT assigned).
  local dol unengaged elastic
  dol="$(awk -v done_t="$trail" -v assign_t="$assign_trail" -v lanes="$LANES" -v amin="$ASSIGN_MIN" 'BEGIN{
    nl=split(lanes, L, / +/); for(i=1;i<=nl;i++) islane[L[i]]=1
    n=split(done_t, D, / +/);  for(i=1;i<=n;i++){ if(D[i]=="")continue; split(D[i],kv,":"); donec[kv[1]]=kv[2]+0 }
    m=split(assign_t, A, / +/); for(i=1;i<=m;i++){ if(A[i]=="")continue; split(A[i],kv,":"); asg[kv[1]]=kv[2]+0 }
    un=""; el=""
    for(w in asg)   if(asg[w]>=amin && (donec[w]+0)==0 && islane[w]) un=un sprintf("%s(%d) ", w, asg[w])
    for(w in donec) if(donec[w]>0   && (asg[w]+0)==0   && islane[w]) el=el sprintf("%s(%d) ", w, donec[w])
    printf "UN|%s\nEL|%s\n", un, el
  }')"
  unengaged="$(echo "$dol" | sed -n 's/^UN|//p' | sed 's/ *$//')"
  elastic="$(echo "$dol"   | sed -n 's/^EL|//p' | sed 's/ *$//')"

  # circular-mill (positive-feedback-trap) reading — additive, never changes rc
  local ml ml_total ml_trails
  ml="$(mill)"
  if [ "$ml" = "NA" ]; then ml_total="na"; ml_trails=""
  else ml_total="${ml%% |*}"; ml_trails="$(echo "${ml#*| }" | sed 's/ *$//')"; fi

  # sematectonic-grounding (marker-vs-artifact) reading — additive, never changes rc
  local gr gr_total gr_grounded gr_pct gr_bare
  gr="$(grounding "$cutoff" < "$CHAT")"
  read -r gr_total gr_grounded gr_pct <<<"$(echo "$gr" | head -1)"
  gr_bare="$(echo "$gr" | sed -n '2p' | sed 's/ *$//')"

  if [ "$JSON" -eq 1 ]; then
    printf '{"regime":"%s","evenness_J":%s,"dominant_share":%s,"dominant_lane":"%s","done_marks":%d,"active_lanes":%d,"window_h":%s,"trail":"%s","no_entry_repellent":%s,"no_entry_lanes":"%s","intended_evenness_J":%s,"assigned_tasks":%d,"owner_trail":"%s","unengaged_specialists":"%s","elastic_generalists":"%s","mill_trails":%s,"mill_detail":"%s","grounded_discharge_pct":%s,"grounded_marks":%d,"sign_based_deposits":"%s"}\n' \
      "$regime" "${J:-0}" "${dom:-0}" "${domlane:-none}" "${total:-0}" "${k:-0}" "$HOURS" "$(echo "$trail" | sed 's/ *$//')" \
      "$nej" "$(echo "$ne_lanes" | sed 's/ *$//')" \
      "${J_assign:--1}" "${as_total:-0}" "$assign_trail" "$unengaged" "$elastic" \
      "$([ "$ml_total" = na ] && echo -1 || echo "${ml_total:-0}")" "$ml_trails" \
      "$([ "${gr_total:-0}" -eq 0 ] && echo -1 || echo "${gr_pct:-0}")" "${gr_grounded:-0}" "$gr_bare"
  else
    echo   "forage: $regime   J=${J} (evenness, 1=perfectly balanced)   dominant=${domlane} ${dom}   marks=${total}/${HOURS}h across ${k} lanes"
    [ -n "$trail" ] && echo "  trail: $trail"
    case "$regime" in
      STAGNATING) echo "  -> the colony is funneling completed work into few trails; the quiet lanes may be DEAD (green+silent). Check the roster." ;;
      n/a)        echo "  -> too few done-marks in the window to measure foraging balance." ;;
    esac
    if [ "$ne_total" = "na" ]; then
      echo "  no-entry: n/a (mesh-promises/jq unavailable — negative-pheromone axis blind)"
    elif [ "${ne_total:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
      echo "  no-entry: clear — no abandoned [taking]s (no repellent trails laid)"
    else
      echo "  no-entry: repellent=${ne_total} abandoned [taking](s) | ${ne_lanes}"
      [ -n "$repelled" ] && echo "  -> repelled (>=${REPEL_MIN}): ${repelled}— foragers re-entering an unrewarding branch; a no-entry signal the [done]-field is blind to."
    fi
    # response-threshold / division-of-labour axis
    if [ "${as_total:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
      echo "  division-of-labour: no owner-assigned [task]s in window — intended-allocation field empty"
    else
      local jatxt="${J_assign}"
      [ "${J_assign}" = "-1" ] && jatxt="n/a (single owner lane)"
      echo "  division-of-labour: intended J=${jatxt} (owner-assignment evenness)   assigned=${as_total}/${HOURS}h across ${k_assign} lanes"
      [ -n "$assign_trail" ] && echo "  owner-trail: $assign_trail"
      if [ -n "$unengaged" ]; then
        echo "  -> unengaged (assigned >=${ASSIGN_MIN}, delivered 0): ${unengaged}— directed stimulus not crossing the lane's threshold; recruitment gap (dead specialist?), the [done]-field is blind to it."
      else
        echo "  engaged: every assigned mind lane delivered >=1 [done] (no unengaged specialist)"
      fi
      [ -n "$elastic" ] && echo "  elastic: ${elastic}— delivering on unassigned work (generalists absorbing overflow; healthy recruitment)."
    fi
    # circular-mill / positive-feedback-trap axis
    if [ "$ml_total" = "na" ]; then
      echo "  mill: n/a (mesh-promises/jq unavailable — positive-feedback-trap axis blind)"
    elif [ "${ml_total:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
      echo "  mill: clear — no open trail re-deposited >=${MILL_MIN}x (no circular pheromone trap)"
    else
      echo "  mill: ${ml_total} circling trail(s) | ${ml_trails}"
      echo "  -> an OPEN claim re-deposited >=${MILL_MIN}x with no [done] = the ant-mill signature (positive feedback, no progress). Escape = inject a DEFECTION: one mind breaks the loop — close it, escalate to the operator, or try a materially different approach."
    fi
    # sematectonic-grounding / marker-vs-artifact axis
    if [ "${gr_total:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
      echo "  grounding: n/a (no [done] deposits in window to measure)"
    else
      echo "  grounding: ${gr_pct}% sematectonic (${gr_grounded}/${gr_total} discharges cite an artifact — path/file/tool/commit)"
      if [ -n "$gr_bare" ]; then
        echo "  -> sign-based (bare-marker, no artifact cite): ${gr_bare}— a [done] clearing a promise on the MARKER alone; the ledger discharges the liability without a trace a reader can verify. (Grassé sematectonic vs sign-based stigmergy; Ledger-State Stigmergy arXiv:2604.03997 2026: 'the trace should BE the operational state'.)"
      fi
    fi
  fi
  exit "$rc"
}

# ── smoke: pure evenness on fixtures + RED-first falsifier ──
run_test() {
  local fail=0
  tmp="$(mktemp -d)"; trap 'rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT
  local ts; ts="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"

  # fixture EVEN: 4 lanes x 3 done-marks each -> J must be ~1.0 (BALANCED)
  local fe="$tmp/even.log"; : >"$fe"
  for L in genome senses health tg; do for i in 1 2 3; do
    echo "$ts  ${L}@mesh-home  ::  [done] fixture-$L-$i: work" >>"$fe"; done; done
  # a prose line that MENTIONS [done] must NOT be counted (substring-scan trap)
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [fyi] genome posted a [done] earlier, discussing it here" >>"$fe"

  # fixture SOLO: one lane holds all 12 -> J=0 (STAGNATING)
  local fs="$tmp/solo.log"; : >"$fs"
  for i in $(seq 1 12); do echo "$ts  genome@mesh-home  ::  [done] fixture-solo-$i: work" >>"$fs"; done

  echo "== fixture EVEN (4 lanes x3) =="
  local jE regE
  jE="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fe" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 "$0" --json)"
  echo "  $jE"
  regE="$(echo "$jE" | grep -oE '"regime":"[A-Za-z/]+"' | cut -d'"' -f4)"
  # 4 lanes counted (prose [fyi] excluded), J>=0.99, BALANCED
  echo "$jE" | grep -q '"active_lanes":4' || { echo "  FAIL: expected 4 active lanes (prose [fyi] leaked in?)"; fail=1; }
  awk -v j="$(echo "$jE" | grep -oE '"evenness_J":[0-9.]+' | cut -d: -f2)" 'BEGIN{exit !(j>=0.99)}' \
    || { echo "  FAIL: even fixture J must be >=0.99"; fail=1; }
  [ "$regE" = "BALANCED" ] || { echo "  FAIL: even fixture must be BALANCED, got $regE"; fail=1; }

  echo "== fixture SOLO (1 lane x12) =="
  local jS regS
  jS="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fs" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 "$0" --json)"
  echo "  $jS"
  regS="$(echo "$jS" | grep -oE '"regime":"[A-Za-z/]+"' | cut -d'"' -f4)"
  echo "$jS" | grep -q '"evenness_J":0' || { echo "  FAIL: solo fixture J must be 0"; fail=1; }
  [ "$regS" = "STAGNATING" ] || { echo "  FAIL: solo fixture must be STAGNATING, got $regS"; fail=1; }

  # RED-FIRST FALSIFIER: neuter the evenness (force J=0) on the EVEN fixture, where dominance is
  # only 0.25 so the verdict is driven by J ALONE. BALANCED MUST flip to STAGNATING — proving the
  # J gate reads the real number, not a constant. (Isolates J: dominance is unchanged.)
  echo "== falsifier: MESH_FORAGE_BREAK=1 (J->0) must flip the EVEN verdict =="
  local regBroken
  regBroken="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fe" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_BREAK=1 "$0" --json | grep -oE '"regime":"[A-Za-z/]+"' | cut -d'"' -f4)"
  if [ "$regBroken" = "BALANCED" ]; then
    echo "  FAIL: even fixture still BALANCED with J neutered to 0 -> the gate is NOT reading J (vacuous)"; fail=1
  else
    echo "  ok: neutered J=0 flips even $regE -> $regBroken (J gate is live)"
  fi

  # n/a: below MIN_MARKS
  echo "== fixture SPARSE (<MIN_MARKS) -> n/a exit 2 =="
  local fsp="$tmp/sparse.log"; echo "$ts  genome@mesh-home  ::  [done] one: work" >"$fsp"
  MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fsp" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 "$0" >/dev/null 2>&1
  [ $? -eq 2 ] || { echo "  FAIL: sparse must exit 2 (n/a)"; fail=1; }
  echo "  ok: sparse -> n/a exit 2"

  # ── NO-ENTRY axis: repellent stub must flag the lane; empty stub must NOT (RED-first) ──
  # Drives the REAL consume-and-bucket path via MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES (a stubbed mesh-promises --json).
  # The EVEN fixture reads BALANCED on the positive field, so the no-entry flag is the ONLY thing the
  # populated-vs-empty stub can change — proving the axis reads .hold_leaks, not a constant.
  echo "== no-entry: populated repellent stub flags the lane =="
  echo '{"hold_leaks":[{"taker":"models"},{"taker":"models"},{"taker":"models"}]}' >"$tmp/hl.json"
  local outNE
  outNE="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fe" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES="cat $tmp/hl.json" "$0")"
  echo "  $(echo "$outNE" | grep -E 'no-entry|repelled' | sed 's/^/  /')"
  echo "$outNE" | grep -q 'no-entry: repellent=3'    || { echo "  FAIL: repellent=3 not reported from stub"; fail=1; }
  echo "$outNE" | grep -Eq 'repelled .*models:3'      || { echo "  FAIL: models lane not flagged repelled"; fail=1; }

  echo "== falsifier: empty repellent stub must NOT flag (axis reads data, not a constant) =="
  echo '{"hold_leaks":[]}' >"$tmp/hl0.json"
  local outNE0
  outNE0="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fe" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES="cat $tmp/hl0.json" "$0")"
  if echo "$outNE0" | grep -q 'repelled'; then
    echo "  FAIL: empty hold_leaks still flags a repelled lane -> no-entry axis is a constant"; fail=1
  else
    echo "  ok: empty repellent -> no flag; populated -> models:3 flagged (no-entry axis is live)"
  fi
  echo "$outNE0" | grep -q 'no-entry: clear' || { echo "  FAIL: empty hold_leaks must read 'no-entry: clear'"; fail=1; }

  echo "== no-entry: unavailable source -> honest n/a, never a faked all-clear =="
  local outNEna
  outNEna="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fe" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES="false" "$0")"
  echo "$outNEna" | grep -q 'no-entry: n/a' || { echo "  FAIL: unavailable source must read 'no-entry: n/a', not clear"; fail=1; }
  echo "  ok: unavailable promises source -> no-entry: n/a"

  # ── RESPONSE-THRESHOLD (division-of-labour) axis ──
  # Fixture: the EVEN done-log (genome/senses/health/tg each deliver 3) + owner-assigned [task]s where
  # genome & senses ARE assigned (and deliver), vpn is assigned 2 but delivers 0 (unengaged specialist),
  # and a prose "owner:" mention must NOT be counted. tg delivers 3 while assigned 0 -> elastic generalist.
  local fd="$tmp/dol.log"; cp "$fe" "$fd"
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [task] a1 — owner: mesh-gen/genome — real assign"      >>"$fd"
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [task] a2 — owner: genome — real assign"               >>"$fd"
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [task] a3 — owner: senses — real assign"               >>"$fd"
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [task] a4 — owner: vpn — assigned, will not deliver"   >>"$fd"
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [task] a5 — owner: vpn — assigned, will not deliver"   >>"$fd"
  echo "$ts  minds@mesh-home  ::  [fyi] discussing the owner: convention, not an assign" >>"$fd"   # prose trap
  echo "== division-of-labour: unengaged specialist flagged, elastic generalist flagged, prose excluded =="
  local jD
  jD="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fd" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 "$0" --json)"
  echo "  $(echo "$jD" | grep -oE '"assigned_tasks":[0-9]+|"unengaged_specialists":"[^"]*"|"elastic_generalists":"[^"]*"|"owner_trail":"[^"]*"')"
  # 5 real assigns counted (prose [fyi] excluded -> not 6)
  echo "$jD" | grep -q '"assigned_tasks":5' || { echo "  FAIL: expected 5 owner-assigned tasks (prose leaked in?)"; fail=1; }
  echo "$jD" | grep -Eq '"unengaged_specialists":"[^"]*vpn\(2\)' || { echo "  FAIL: vpn(2) not flagged unengaged (assigned 2, delivered 0)"; fail=1; }
  echo "$jD" | grep -Eq '"elastic_generalists":"[^"]*tg\(3\)'    || { echo "  FAIL: tg(3) not flagged elastic (delivered 3, assigned 0)"; fail=1; }

  echo "== falsifier: raise ASSIGN_MIN above vpn's 2 -> vpn MUST drop from unengaged (gate reads count) =="
  local jD3
  jD3="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fd" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_ASSIGN_MIN=3 "$0" --json)"
  if echo "$jD3" | grep -Eq '"unengaged_specialists":"[^"]*vpn'; then
    echo "  FAIL: vpn still flagged unengaged at ASSIGN_MIN=3 (>2) -> the count gate is a constant"; fail=1
  else
    echo "  ok: ASSIGN_MIN=3 drops vpn(2) from unengaged (assign-count gate is live)"
  fi

  echo "== falsifier: drop vpn from MESH_FORAGE_LANES -> non-lane owner MUST NOT forge a starvation flag =="
  local jDL
  jDL="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fd" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_LANES="genome senses tg" "$0" --json)"
  if echo "$jDL" | grep -Eq '"unengaged_specialists":"[^"]*vpn'; then
    echo "  FAIL: vpn flagged unengaged though not in MESH_FORAGE_LANES -> lane guard is vacuous"; fail=1
  else
    echo "  ok: owner off the lane roster is not flagged (junk/operator/doc owners cannot forge starvation)"
  fi

  # ── CIRCULAR-MILL axis: an OPEN slug re-deposited >=MILL_MIN times flags; <MILL_MIN must NOT (RED-first) ──
  # The open-set + slug come from the stubbed mesh-promises; the CHAT fixture controls the re-deposit COUNT.
  # The EVEN done-field reads BALANCED, so the mill flag is the ONLY thing the count can change — proving
  # the axis reads the reinforcement count, not a constant.
  echo '{"hold_leaks":[{"taker":"genome","slug":"stuck-thing"}]}' >"$tmp/mp.json"
  local fm="$tmp/mill.log"; cp "$fe" "$fm"
  for m in "[taking] stuck-thing: retrying" "[verify] stuck-thing: still open" "[fyi] stuck-thing: circling back" "[taking] stuck-thing: re-taking"; do
    echo "$ts  genome@mesh-home  ::  $m" >>"$fm"; done   # 4 re-deposits of ONE open slug, never a [done]
  echo "== mill: open slug re-deposited 4x (>=MILL_MIN) flags a circling trail =="
  local jM
  jM="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fm" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES="cat $tmp/mp.json" "$0" --json)"
  echo "  $(echo "$jM" | grep -oE '"mill_trails":[0-9-]+|"mill_detail":"[^"]*"')"
  echo "$jM" | grep -q '"mill_trails":1'                       || { echo "  FAIL: expected 1 circling trail from 4 re-deposits"; fail=1; }
  echo "$jM" | grep -Eq '"mill_detail":"[^"]*genome/stuck-thing:4' || { echo "  FAIL: genome/stuck-thing:4 not reported"; fail=1; }

  echo "== falsifier: raise MILL_MIN above the re-deposit count -> the trail MUST drop (gate reads the count) =="
  local jM9
  jM9="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fm" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_MILL_MIN=9 MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES="cat $tmp/mp.json" "$0" --json)"
  if echo "$jM9" | grep -Eq '"mill_trails":[1-9]'; then
    echo "  FAIL: still flags a mill at MILL_MIN=9 (>4 re-deposits) -> the count gate is a constant"; fail=1
  else
    echo "  ok: MILL_MIN=9 drops the 4x trail (mill count gate is live)"
  fi

  echo "== mill: unavailable source -> honest n/a, never a faked all-clear =="
  local outMna
  outMna="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fm" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_PROMISES="false" "$0")"
  echo "$outMna" | grep -q 'mill: n/a' || { echo "  FAIL: unavailable source must read 'mill: n/a', not clear"; fail=1; }
  echo "  ok: unavailable promises source -> mill: n/a"

  # ── SEMATECTONIC-GROUNDING axis: a [done] that CITES an artifact is grounded; a bare-marker [done]
  #    (no path/tool/commit token) is sign-based. RED-first: the classifier MUST see the bare one, and the
  #    break hook must be able to blind it — proving it reads the text, not a constant. ──
  local fg="$tmp/ground.log"; : >"$fg"
  echo "$ts  genome@mesh-home  ::  [done] axis-a: wrote docs/reviews/thing.md"       >>"$fg"   # cites a path
  echo "$ts  senses@mesh-home  ::  [done] axis-b: patched mesh-situation gate"       >>"$fg"   # cites a tool
  echo "$ts  health@mesh-home  ::  [done] axis-c: fix landed, commit verified"       >>"$fg"   # commit keyword
  echo "$ts  vpn@mesh-home  ::  [done] axis-d self-healed and everything is fine"    >>"$fg"   # BARE marker, no cite
  echo "== grounding: 3/4 discharges cite an artifact; the bare one is flagged sign-based =="
  local jG
  jG="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fg" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 "$0" --json)"
  echo "  $(echo "$jG" | grep -oE '"grounded_discharge_pct":[0-9-]+|"grounded_marks":[0-9]+|"sign_based_deposits":"[^"]*"')"
  echo "$jG" | grep -q '"grounded_marks":3'                      || { echo "  FAIL: expected 3 grounded discharges (path/tool/commit cited)"; fail=1; }
  echo "$jG" | grep -Eq '"sign_based_deposits":"[^"]*vpn/axis-d' || { echo "  FAIL: bare vpn/axis-d not flagged sign-based"; fail=1; }

  echo "== falsifier: MESH_FORAGE_GROUND_BREAK=1 forces all-grounded -> the bare one MUST vanish (classifier reads text) =="
  local jGB
  jGB="$(MESH_FORAGE_CHAT="$fg" MESH_FORAGE_HOURS=99999 MESH_FORAGE_GROUND_BREAK=1 "$0" --json)"
  if echo "$jGB" | grep -Eq '"sign_based_deposits":"[^"]*vpn'; then
    echo "  FAIL: bare vpn still flagged with break=1 -> the sign-based flag isn't reading the classifier"; fail=1
  else
    echo "  ok: break=1 blinds the classifier (all grounded); real path flags vpn/axis-d (grounding axis is live)"
  fi

  echo
  if [ "$fail" -eq 0 ]; then echo "mesh-forage --test: PASS"; else echo "mesh-forage --test: FAIL"; fi
  return "$fail"
}

if [ "${exec_test:-0}" = "1" ]; then run_test; exit $?; fi
run
